# Grid A — S11 Boolean / Existence (retry mechanism wired)
#
# Targets: ShapeBoolean. Answer must name the retry budget to
# prove it reached the enforcement site, not just speculate.
#
# Ground truth (internal/orchestrator/orchestrator.go): Phase 1
# dispatches analyze with fail-loud retry governed by
# MaxRetriesPerStage. If emit_analysis is never called, StageOutput
# carries an Error, the retry loop reruns analyze up to budget,
# then terminates. Positive anchor requires both the budget name
# and the tool name. Negative anchor blocks the "silent fallback"
# failure mode — codrax deliberately does NOT silently fall back to
# a zero-value AnalysisIR.
ID="s11b"
NAME="boolean — is there a retry wired for missing emit_analysis?"
QUESTION="Is there a retry mechanism wired to the analyze stage when emit_analysis is never called? If yes, what is the retry budget parameter called?"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="MaxRetriesPerStage emit_analysis"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="silent fallback zero-value default"
